This directory CANNOT BE COMPILED BY THE TOOLCHAIN IN THIS CHECKOUT.

  SDK 8.0.401  rejects  <LangVersion>13</LangVersion>  with
  CSC : error CS1617: Invalid option '13' for /langversion.

It is here by explicit ruling, and three rules attach to it:

  1. It is EXCLUDED from every compile-status gate. A sweep that builds
     `find . -name '*.csproj'` must skip this one, and must skip it by
     READING THIS MARKER or the `CsFixtureVerifiable` property, never by
     name-matching and never by swallowing the failure.

  2. `cs-oracle` MAY NOT BLESS A GOLDEN FROM IT. The NuGet-pinned Roslyn
     4.12.0 accepts LangVersion 13; the SDK in this checkout does not. An
     adjudicator that runs ahead of the toolchain can freeze an expectation
     for a program nobody here can build, and that expectation is then the
     spec. The oracle may PARSE these files to check the grammar handles
     C# 13 syntax. It may not author facts from them.

  3. Skipping it SILENTLY is worse than not having it. Whatever excludes it
     must say so in its output.

Machine-readable signals, both present:
  * this file, `NOT-VERIFIABLE-HERE`, in the project directory;
  * `<CsFixtureVerifiable>false</CsFixtureVerifiable>` in the .csproj,
    readable with `dotnet msbuild -getProperty:CsFixtureVerifiable`
    WITHOUT invoking the compiler, so querying it does not trip CS1617.

To verify this project at all, a .NET 9 SDK (or any SDK shipping Roslyn
4.12+) is required. That is an environmental fact about the checkout, in
exactly the sense BUILDING-A-PARSER.md section 7 means it, and it must be
classified as environmental rather than reported as a gap.
